  "created": "2021-05-14T20:29:43.669Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "During the pandemic I joined an entirely virtual startup, we've not actually met in person yet. I discovered a few of my coworkers have vrchat accounts. I'd like to be able to hang out with them and create a virtual office for us. But I'd also like to be able to avoid mixing my private account with my work account. \nThe product we're building visualizes complex multi dimensional data, so it would be amazing  to be able to riff on bring that data to 3D with then in VRChat, but we'd want this stuff to be private. \nIdeally I'd like be able to have multiple identities in VRChat and perhaps transfer my user level between my identites so that I don't always have to start from scratch again. \nMy request is that the VRChat team consider this use case of multiple social identities and accounts and a way to allow a user to escalate their trust for world creation, perhaps a vrchat ++ account? \nI already pay for a vrchat+ account, I'd pay for a second, if it would allow me to quickly create new content as a new identity, if that was possible but I'm not sure how",
